cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Se usi mzLab nella didattica o in una pubblicazione, citalo come segue. / If you use mzLab in teaching or in a publication, please cite it as below."
title: "mzLab: a browser-based teaching tool for LC-MS data analysis and the search for transformation products"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Cristaudo
    given-names: Federico
    affiliation: "Università degli Studi di Torino"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/XXXX-XXXX-XXXX-XXXX"  # DA COMPILARE da Federico
repository-code: "https://github.com/Freeesta/mzlab"
url: "https://freeesta.github.io/mzlab/"
license: MIT
version: "0.1.0"
# date-released: "AAAA-MM-GG"  # DA COMPILARE alla prima release
# doi: "10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX"  # DA COMPILARE dopo la prima release su Zenodo (vedi docs/zenodo.md)
keywords:
  - mass spectrometry
  - LC-MS
  - transformation products
  - chemical education
  - non-target screening
  - WebAssembly
abstract: "mzLab is a free teaching program that runs entirely in the web browser. Students explore real LC-MS data (triple quadrupole at unit resolution, plus high-resolution Orbitrap and Q-TOF files) to search for the transformation products of a pollutant; the program shows the data and does not give the answers. No installation, no account, no tracking: files never leave the computer."
